  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A 3-star hotel right in the centre of Menton, at 5 rue de la République, 50 metres from the beaches according to its website and 800 m from the station, reachable on foot. It has six floors of rooms, two lifts, a brasserie restaurant "M-Sens" on the ground floor and, on the 7th floor, a bar and a rooftop with panoramic views.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>The FAQ of the hotel's official website answers the question "Do you accept animals?": the hotel accepts animals, except in the restaurant, at no extra charge. It specifies further on that pets are not admitted in the restaurant room, but are welcome in the other areas of the hotel. The breakfast buffet is served in the restaurant room, from 6am to 10:30am; a continental breakfast can be delivered to the room from 7am to 11am, for a supplement (the site gives €2 per person in one answer and €5 in another).</p>
      <p>The hotel's garage is paid (€18 to €24 depending on the period, maximum height 1.80 m, video surveillance); the town hall car park (23 rue de la République) and the Saint-Roch car park (10 avenue Félix Faure) are a 3-minute walk away.</p>
      <p>Check before you go: the hotel's website specifies neither the size nor the number of dogs admitted; call the hotel (04 92 41 81 81) before booking if your dog is large or if you have several animals.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: only the M-Sens restaurant room is off-limits to dogs. The hotel does not say whether the 7th-floor rooftop (bar open 5pm to 11pm, rooftop restaurant from May to September) accepts them: ask at reception.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The hotel's website announces the beaches at 50 metres. To walk your dog along the seafront, check the rule for Menton's beaches in the guide.</p>
    </div>

